---
source: src/main.rs
expression: "render_help_snapshot(&[])"
---
Inspect webhooks, replay failures, and expose localhost from your terminal

Usage: hooklistener [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  listen         Forward events from a debug endpoint to a local URL
  tunnel         Expose a local HTTP server on a public Hooklistener URL
  endpoint       Manage debug endpoints and their captured requests
  static-tunnel  Reserve and manage static tunnel slugs
  anon           Create temporary endpoints and tunnels (no login required)
  cases          Run saved replay cases against a target
  share          Create, inspect, and revoke public links to captured requests
  monitor        Create and inspect uptime monitors
  login          Sign in with the device flow
  logout         Sign out and delete the stored token
  org            List organizations and set the default one
  config         Show and set CLI configuration
  diagnostics    Write a diagnostic bundle for support
  clean-logs     Delete old log files
  completions    Print a shell completion script
  update         Update hooklistener to the latest release
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
      --json               Output supported command responses or event streams as JSON
      --color <COLOR>      Styling policy for human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto,
                           always, never]
      --yes                Confirm destructive commands without an interactive prompt
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn,
                           error]
      --log-dir <DIR>      Directory for log files
      --log-stdout         Also write logs to stdout

COMMAND GROUPS:
  Capture and delivery: listen, tunnel, endpoint, static-tunnel, anon
  Review and automation: cases, share, monitor
  Account and settings: login, logout, org, config
  Maintenance: diagnostics, clean-logs, completions, update

COMMON WORKFLOWS:
  Sign in:
    hooklistener login

  Forward an existing debug endpoint:
    hooklistener listen <endpoint-slug> --target http://localhost:3000

  Expose a local HTTP server:
    hooklistener tunnel --port 3000

  Create and inspect hosted captures:
    hooklistener endpoint create <name>
    hooklistener endpoint list-requests <endpoint-id>
